for the orchestrator's checkpoint + `done`/`commit_ack`.\n\nTree verified byte-identical to candidate `3780d471` before and after every mutant (restores from a `.temp` copy, never `git checkout` — the whole rework is uncommitted).\n\n## G-A — the `ownerAttester` seam: justified, one residual\n\nThe seam holds on every axis you named:\n\n- **No production path reassigns or observes it.** Unexported, under `internal/`, read at one site (`os.go:48`). And it's the *fifth* instance of an idiom this package already carries: `failDuplicate`/`failInvalid`/`failPrecondition`/`failIntegrity` have been production `var` function values since rev 1, swapped by `TestMain` for the same reason.\n- **No parallelism, structurally.** Zero `t.Parallel` in the package, and four `os_test.go` tests call `t.Setenv`, which *panics* if the test ever parallelizes. Repo-wide `-race` green; provider also green under `-race -count=2` and `-race -shuffle=on`.\n- **Seam-free alternatives don't dominate.** An `OSSystem.attester` field just moves the same unkilled target into `Inspect`'s nil-fallback. Windows-only coverage is seam-free but regresses evidence from executed to compiled.\n\n**But its own comment — \"Production code never reassigns it\" — is unenforced, and I measured what that costs:**\n\n| Mutant | Result |\n| --- | ---: |\n| production `init()` → attest every file as the operator | **SURVIVED** |\n| production `init()` → attest uid 0 | KILLED (`TestOSSystemEndToEnd`) |\n| same weakening written into `fileOwnerUID`, no seam | KILLED (`TestFileOwnerUIDRefusesWithoutMetadata`) |\n\nOne weakening, killed at the natural site, survivable through the new seam — because the attestation test calls `fileOwnerUID` directly and nothing pins `ownerAttester == fileOwnerUID`. Non-blocking: unreachable by any caller, requires writing the bypass into the package under review, and the uid-0 shape from LOGBOOK 0230 *is* killed. Filed as **F18** with a four-line closer.\n\n## G-B — 80 killed / 83 measured, zero resurrections\n\n- **45 of round 3's kills re-run — 45 still killed.** Nothing was loosened.\n- **F11 closed properly:** B1/B2/H4/B5 all redden; the reverse check lists the 18 orphaned sites.\n- **F12:** rows 40/43/44/47/48/50 redden. Row 49 (`Geteuid`→`Getuid`) survives — environment-equivalent, `euid=502 uid=502` probed, reported as unknown not inferred.\n- **F13's fix is the right shape:** each deletion-form kill fails by naming the *wrong downstream* detail.\n- **F14, F16, F17 closed. F15 closed at 4 of 5 return sites.**\n\nTwo of last round's five \"equivalent\" survivors are now **proven**, not reasoned: `scalar.Digest` is only producible via `SHA256Digest` (lowercase hex) or `ParseDigest` (rejects non-lowercase), so rows 36/37/38 are equivalent by construction. Rows 42/45 stay reasoned.\n\n## Two more findings, both one-liners, handed to the story\n\n**F19** — `return out, err` at the `plugin_dirs` absolute-path refusal (`provider.go:338`) survives; `TestDiscoverRefusesRelativePluginDir` gives its absolute dirs *empty* entry lists, so `out` is nil at the refusal regardless of index. I proved non-equivalence rather than asserting it: mutant + one planted `ax-provider-foo` → **1 candidate leaks alongside the refusal**, against `doc.go` and `README.md:399`.\n\n**F20** — `GOOS=windows go vet` genuinely type-checks `os_windows_test.go` (verified by planting a type error and watching vet report it), but `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs only `go test/vet/build` on ubuntu — **no cross-compile step**. `os_windows.go` and its test are invisible to CI; breaking either leaves CI green. The check present but uncalled, one level up.\n\nBounds unchanged: no production caller of `internal/provider` exists anywhere in the tree; Windows behavior is compile-verified, not executed; the `Inspect`→`ReadFile` TOCTOU window is unprobed.","ttft_ms":1501,"type":"result","duration_ms":1085730,"uuid":"1c32ef5a-44b7-4264-ba97-ab48b96d0c82","ttft_stream_ms":1132,"time_to_request_m